<FILENAME>ea179143ex99-1_wearable.htm
<DESCRIPTION>PRESS RELEASE ISSUED BY WEARABLE DEVICES LTD. DATED MAY 23, 2023, TITLED "WEARABLE DEVICES GRANTED 180-DAY EXTENSION BY NASDAQ TO REGAIN COMPLIANCE WITH MINIMUM BID REQUIREMENT."
<TEXT>
<HTML>
<HEAD>
     <TITLE></TITLE>
</HEAD>
<BODY STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif">

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: right; background-color: white"><B>Exhibit 99.1</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center; background-color: white">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center; background-color: white"><B>Wearable Devices Granted
180-Day Extension by Nasdaq to Regain Compliance with Minimum Bid Requirement</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center; background-color: white"><B>No Immediate Effect
on Nasdaq Listing or Trading of the Company&rsquo;s Ordinary Shares</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">YOKNEAM ILLIT, ISRAEL, May 23, 2023 (GLOBE
NEWSWIRE) -- Wearable Devices Ltd. (Nasdaq: WLDS, WLDSW) (&ldquo;Wearable Devices&rdquo; or the &ldquo;Company&rdquo;), a technology
growth company developing AI-powered touchless sensing wearables, today announced that it has received a notification letter from
Nasdaq Stock Market LLC (&ldquo;Nasdaq&rdquo;) that the Company has been granted an additional 180-day compliance period, or until
November 20, 2023 to regain compliance with Nasdaq&rsquo;s minimum bid price rule.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">Nasdaq&rsquo;s determination is based on the Company
meeting the continued listing requirement for market value of publicly held shares and all other applicable requirements for initial listing
on the Nasdaq Capital Market, with the exception of the bid price requirement, and the Company&rsquo;s written notice of its intention
to cure the deficiency during the second compliance period and if necessary, by effecting a reverse stock split.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">In a notification letter dated November 23, 2022,
Nasdaq had informed the Company that, based on the previous 30 consecutive business days, the Company&rsquo;s ordinary shares no longer
met the minimum $1.00 bid price per share requirement. Therefore, in accordance with Nasdaq&rsquo;s Listing Rules, the Company was provided
180 calendar days, or until May 22, 2023, to regain compliance.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; background-color: white">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; background-color: white">If at any time before
November 20, 2023, the closing bid price of the Company&rsquo;s ordinary shares is at least $1.00 per share for a minimum of 10 consecutive
business days, the Company will regain compliance with this Nasdaq rule and this matter will be closed.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; background-color: white">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; background-color: white">This current notification
from Nasdaq has no immediate effect on the listing or trading of the Company&rsquo;s ordinary shares, which will continue to trade on
the Nasdaq Capital Market under the symbol &ldquo;WLDS.&rdquo;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; background-color: white">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; background-color: white"><B>About&nbsp;Wearable Devices&nbsp;Ltd.</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; background-color: white">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="text-align: justify; font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; background-color: white">Wearable Devices Ltd. (the &ldquo;Company&rdquo;)
is a growth company developing AI-based neural input interface technology for the B2C and B2B markets. The Company&rsquo;s flagship product,
the Mudra Band for Apple Watch, integrates innovative AI-based technology and algorithms into a functional, stylish wristband that utilizes
proprietary sensors to identify subtle finger and wrist movements allowing the user to &ldquo;touchlessly&rdquo; interact with connected
devices. The Company also markets a B2B product, the Mudra Inspire, which utilizes the same technology and functions as the Mudra Band
and is available to businesses on a licensing basis. Wearable Devices is committed to creating disruptive, industry leading technology
that leverages AI and proprietary algorithms, software, and hardware to set the input standard for the Metaverse, one of the most rapidly
expanding landscapes in the tech industry. The Company&rsquo;s common stock trades on the Nasdaq market under the symbol &ldquo;WLDS&rdquo;.
For more information, please visit&nbsp;https://www.wearabledevices.co.il/.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; background-color: white">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; background-color: white"></P>

